{"uid":"e77636fadeaa6949","name":"test_an_unknown_task_id_exhausts_the_ladder_and_still_refuses_the_move","fullName":"tests.test_unsatisfiable_criteria#test_an_unknown_task_id_exhausts_the_ladder_and_still_refuses_the_move","historyId":"da9521c37da39fb7f01afe5f1dad3590","time":{"start":1791919646037,"stop":1791919646454,"duration":417},"description":"v0.13 task 005: same cutover as the no-reason case above -- an\n    unresolvable `task_id` is carried back through the SAME re-ask ladder\n    (`\"not found\"` on every `contract.violation` event, never a `log`\n    message the old pre-cutover assertion grepped) rather than aborting on\n    the first offence. With no budget ceiling here (`_run_resumed`'s\n    default `iterations=15`), the worker loop keeps self-looping on\n    `no_verdict_yet` every pass -- three genuinely stuck passes (each its\n    own full ladder) still trips the PRE-EXISTING `stagnation_exhausted`\n    guard exactly as a silent hat would (this task adds no escape hatch\n    from that). Since task 012 (`abdc914`) the guard on the (default) last\n    approach pauses and escalates rather than ending `failed` -- asserted\n    here via `_run_resumed_until_paused` (task 042, steer 004) -- never\n    `\"aborted\"`.","descriptionHtml":"<p>v0.13 task 005: same cutover as the no-reason case above -- an<br />\nunresolvable <code>task_id</code> is carried back through the SAME re-ask ladder<br />\n(<code>&quot;not found&quot;</code> on every <code>contract.violation</code> event, never a <code>log</code><br />\nmessage the old pre-cutover assertion grepped) rather than aborting on<br />\nthe first offence. With no budget ceiling here (<code>_run_resumed</code>'s<br />\ndefault <code>iterations=15</code>), the worker loop keeps self-looping on<br />\n<code>no_verdict_yet</code> every pass -- three genuinely stuck passes (each its<br />\nown full ladder) still trips the PRE-EXISTING <code>stagnation_exhausted</code><br />\nguard exactly as a silent hat would (thi